{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdshEk1mML3iBkTcNX2xG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: APPROVED\n\nAll five verification points are closed:\n\n1. **Dedup by turn ID — yes.** `Confirm-PipelineTaskReady.ps1` replaces the list with a hashtable keyed `[string]$turn.id`, so a turn carrying several matching content entries is recorded once.\n2. **Zero fails, one-or-many selects earliest — yes.** `$matchingTurns.Count -eq 0` throws; otherwise `Sort-Object` on `completedAt` then `id` picks `[0]`, deterministic and independent of the order turns appear in the read.\n3. **Tests cover both cases — yes.** The `duplicate-delivery-intake` block builds two completed turns emitted in reverse order (`turn-2`, then `turn-1`), each with two identical matching content entries, and asserts `turn-1` is chosen and the state reaches `plan_requested`. That exercises duplicate turns, duplicate content, and the sort rather than array position.\n4. **`ALREADY_DELIVERED` — yes.** `Complete-PipelineBoundary.ps1` returns the delivery summary without the message once state is `plan_requested`; it re-emits only while `task_ready_pending`, which is correct since delivery is not yet confirmed and repeats are now idempotent. `Test-ProjectContracts.ps1` pins the string.\n5. **`restore-required.json` before the phase-one marker — yes.** It is written ahead of `Test-PipelineCompactionPhaseOne` and `codex-phase1.json`, so the re-run short-circuit can never fire without the restore checklist already on disk.\n\nThe prior blocker is genuinely closed: a retried send now resolves to the earliest completed turn instead of stranding the task, and `Complete` no longer hands the controller a message to send again after confirmation.\n\nBLOCKING FINDINGS:\n- None.\n\nNONBLOCKING FINDINGS:\n- **Verify `completedAt` against a real `read_thread` payload before the smoke test.** The sort key is a hard `[double]$_.completedAt` cast. The fixture models it as a number (`100 + $turnNumber`), but if Codex App emits an ISO-8601 string, or omits the field on some turns, the cast (or StrictMode property lookup) throws — and because `task_ready_pending` exits only to `plan_requested`, that failure is not operator-recoverable without editing the saved receipt. Dropping the cast (`Sort-Object completedAt, id`) is type-agnostic and removes the risk regardless of what the API returns. Same standing caveat applies to `app_read.thread.id`, `turns[].items[].content[].codexDelegation.input`, and `captured_at`: all are asserted only by hand-built fixtures.\n- A validation failure in `Test-PipelineCompactionPhaseOne` now leaves `restore-required.json` on disk without `codex-phase1.json`. Harmless — the next run rewrites it, and the combination is unambiguous — but worth knowing when reading a failed runtime directory.\n- Unbounded `$stdoutTask.Wait()` / `$stderrTask.Wait()` after a bounded `WaitForExit` in `Invoke-CodexThreadUnarchive`, `Invoke-CodexThreadArchive`, and `Invoke-CodexNodeClient`; `Kill()` is not `Kill($true)`, so no process-tree termination as plan Task 3 Step 5 requires.\n- Nothing verifies the four roles were actually App-archived, or that threads are idle, before phase one CLI-unarchives and compacts (spec §6.1 step 2). A missed archive surfaces as a 600 s compaction failure rather than a fast error.\n- All boundary idempotency state lives in git-ignored `.pipeline/runtime/`. Wiping it at `compacting` recompacts all four roles; wiping it at `task_ready_pending`/`plan_requested` makes the `Confirm`/`Complete` early-exit paths throw on a missing file.\n- `Resolve-CodexExecutable` selects by `LastWriteTimeUtc` rather than version; the Claude resolver next door parses semver. Only one candidate exists in the test, so ordering is unverified.\n- `Get-ClaudeCompactionOutcome` still gates `not_needed` on the exact upstream string `'Not enough messages to compact.'`, and `$sawCompacting` is set by any event with `status -eq 'compacting'` rather than by correlation.\n- `Invoke-CodexThreadUnarchive` and `Invoke-CodexThreadArchive` remain near-identical ~55-line blocks.\n- `Test-ProjectContracts.ps1` still verifies behavior by regex over script source; those assertions pass on a comment. No test drives `Invoke-PipelineBoundary.ps1` or `Complete-PipelineBoundary.ps1` end to end, so `-Force`, per-role receipt reuse, corrupted saved receipts, and the Claude-receipt reuse branch stay uncovered.\n- `task_ready_pending` still has no path to `blocked`. With duplicates now idempotent the practical stranding case is gone, but a genuinely lost Manager thread has no state to land in and no audited recovery.\n- The heartbeat is written once per role, before that role's work, so a hang inside a single 600 s compaction leaves a stale `running` marker rather than a liveness signal."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":77620,"cache_read_input_tokens":292061,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":77620},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"32aaea71-de6b-4a82-a2af-740b042871ec","uuid":"c496bb17-78d3-42db-ab1d-423a7493c5f5","timestamp":"2026-08-09T19:04:47.646Z","request_id":"req_011CdshEi99vktSJRhdtuRXu"}
